  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Friday)\nIssued at 1154 PM CST Fri Nov 27 2026\n\nLooking ahead to next work week, our synoptic pattern will initially \nbe characterized by zonal flow aloft, with relatively quiet weather \nand warmer temperatures in the 60s. Winds will be breezy again out \nof the southwest on Monday, but nowhere near as bad as what will \nhave occurred in days prior. As we approach Wed-Thu, long range \nmodels are honing in on a low pressure system moving onto the west \ncoast and advancing towards the Plains. As it does so, improved deep-\nlayer moisture and increasing lift are currently anticipated to \nreach the region. Low to medium chances for precipitation may return \nas a result, and is favored to remain rain for now. We will have to \nkeep an eye on any dry slot that may quickly impinge upon our \nmoisture, and on the flip side may need to watch for wrap around \nmoisture to provide another round of precip opportunity later Thu. \nExact track and timing of the low are still in question, along with \njust how much precip we may receive. Otherwise, it looks like we \ncould have another cool down behind a cold front late next week, \nwith potential for active weather to return in the first week of \nDecember.\n\nHarrel",
